Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: You should not take venlafaxine if you are allergic to it or to desvenlafaxine (Pristiq).
Do not use venlafaxine if you have used an MAO inhibitor in the past 14 days. A dangerous drug interaction could occur. MAO inhibitors include isocarboxazid, linezolid, methylene blue injection, phenelzine, and tranylcypromine.
Tell your doctor if you also use stimulant medicine, opioid medicine, herbal products, or medicine for depression, mental illness, Parkinson's disease, migraine headaches, serious infections, or prevention of nausea and vomiting. An interaction with venlafaxine could cause a serious condition called serotonin syndrome.
To make sure venlafaxine is safe for you, tell your doctor if you have ever had:
- bipolar disorder (manic depression);
- heart disease, high blood pressure, high cholesterol or triglycerides, or a stroke;
- diabetes;
- lung disease;
- glaucoma;
- a thyroid disorder;
- a seizure;
- sexual problems;
- bleeding problems;
- low blood levels of sodium; or
- liver or kidney disease.
Triplet: ["Venlafaxine", "requires disclosure of", "liver disease"]

The relation 'requires disclosure of' in the triplet is defined as 'Patients should inform their doctor if they have a history of the medical condition specified by the object entity before taking the subject drug.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'should inform doctor about': Patients taking the subject drug should tell their doctor about the condition or circumstance specified by the object entity.
B. 'requires monitoring of': Patients taking the subject drug may need the medical test or monitoring specified by the object entity.
C. 'can occur with': The subject drug can be present in individuals who also have the condition specified by the object entity.
D. 'mimics symptoms of': The subject condition or drug may present symptoms that resemble those of the medical condition specified by the object entity.
E. 'use with caution in': The subject drug may be unsafe or require medical supervision for patients who have the condition or characteristic specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
